Obsidian Study Flow publishes its native plugin, QuickAdd scripts, configuration, documentation,
original demo PDF and diagrams under MIT. It grew from a personal learning workflow.

It depends on independently maintained third-party projects:
- QuickAdd by Christian Houmann: https://github.com/chhoumann/quickadd
- PDF++ by Ryota Ushio: https://github.com/RyotaUshio/obsidian-pdf-plus
- Spaced Repetition by Stephen Mwangi and contributors:
  https://github.com/st3v3nmw/obsidian-spaced-repetition
- Optional Obsidian Web Clipper: https://github.com/obsidianmd/obsidian-clipper

No third-party plugin binaries are redistributed in the repository or starter ZIP.
Install them from Obsidian's community plugin browser. Their licenses remain their own.
Obsidian is a separate application: https://obsidian.md. This is a community project,
not an official Obsidian product. Screenshots use only the original demo vault.

Development-only compatibility fixture:
tests/fixtures/sr-1.15.4/parser.ts is from Obsidian Spaced Repetition 1.15.4
by Stephen Mwangi and contributors, under MIT. Its license and provenance are
included beside the fixture. Only imports are adapted to the test environment.
The fixture, clozecraft and other development dependencies are excluded from
native plugin and example ZIPs.
